Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBexpanse_map_t\fR is an ordered, dynamic map from 64-bit unsigned integer keys
(\fBuint64_t\fR) to 64-bit values (\fBuint64_t\fR), representing a modernized
clean-room equivalent of JudyL.
.PP
Values are stored directly in single-machine-word \fBValueSlot\fRs inside leaf
arrays, allowing direct in-place mutation through slot pointers without tree
re-traversal.
.SH QUICK REFERENCE
.nf
.ta 32n 45n
\fBOperation\fR	\fBFunction\fR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create / Destroy	expanse_map_new, expanse_map_free
Clear Container	expanse_map_clear
Insert / Get / Delete	expanse_map_insert, expanse_map_get, expanse_map_remove
Direct Slot Pointer	expanse_map_slot, expanse_map_ins_slot
Size & Byte Accounting	expanse_map_len, expanse_map_mem_used
First / Last Entry	expanse_map_first, expanse_map_last
Forward Navigation	expanse_map_next_after, expanse_map_next_at_or_after
Reverse Navigation	expanse_map_prev_before, expanse_map_prev_at_or_before
Rank (Count < Key)	expanse_map_count_below, expanse_map_count_range
Select (Nth Entry)	expanse_map_by_count (1-indexed rank)
Batched Prefetch	expanse_map_get_batch (SIMD/MLP)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <expanse.h>

int main(void) {
    expanse_map_t *map = expanse_map_new();

    /* Insert keys and values */
    expanse_map_insert(map, 1000, 42, NULL);

    /* Direct in-place mutation via ValueSlot pointer */
    uint64_t *slot = expanse_map_ins_slot(map, 2000);
    *slot = 99;  /* In-place write without additional lookup */

    /* Point query */
    uint64_t val;
    if (expanse_map_get(map, 1000, &val)) {
        printf("Key 1000 -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);
    }

    /* Sorted range traversal */
    uint64_t k, v;
    if (expanse_map_first(map, &k, &v)) {
        do {
            printf("  %" PRIu64 " => %" PRIu64 "\\n", k, v);
        } while (expanse_map_next_after(map, k, &k, &v));
    }

    expanse_map_free(map);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Lifecycle
.TP
.BI "expanse_map_t *expanse_map_new(void);"
Allocates and initializes a new empty map.
.TP
.BI "void expanse_map_free(expanse_map_t *" map ");"
Frees the map and all internal nodes. Passing NULL is a no-op.
.TP
.BI "void expanse_map_clear(expanse_map_t *" map ");"
Removes all key-value pairs from the map.
.SS Mutations & Queries
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_insert(expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t " key ","
.BI "                        uint64_t " value ", uint64_t *" old_out ");"
Stores \fIkey\fR -> \fIvalue\fR. If \fIkey\fR existed, writes previous value to
\fIold_out\fR (if non-NULL) and returns \fBfalse\fR; returns \fBtrue\fR if new.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_get(const expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t " key ","
.BI "                     uint64_t *" value_out ");"
Looks up \fIkey\fR. On success, writes value to \fIvalue_out\fR (if non-NULL)
and returns \fBtrue\fR; returns \fBfalse\fR if absent.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_remove(expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t " key ","
.BI "                        uint64_t *" old_out ");"
Removes \fIkey\fR. Writes removed value to \fIold_out\fR (if non-NULL).
Returns \fBtrue\fR if found and removed, \fBfalse\fR if absent.
.TP
.BI "uint64_t *expanse_map_slot(expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t " key ");"
Returns a direct writable pointer to the value slot for \fIkey\fR, or NULL if
absent.
.TP
.BI "uint64_t *expanse_map_ins_slot(expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t " key ");"
Inserts \fIkey\fR with initial value 0 if absent (preserving existing value if
present) and returns a writable pointer to its value slot.
.SS Slot Pointer Invalidation Contract
Pointers returned by \fBexpanse_map_slot\fR and \fBexpanse_map_ins_slot\fR
remain valid \fBONLY until the next structural mutation\fR of the map
(\fIinsert\fR, \fIremove\fR, \fIclear\fR, or \fIfree\fR).
.SS Ordered Navigation
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_first(const expanse_map_t *" "map" ", uint64_t *"
.BI "key_out" ","
.BI "                       uint64_t *" value_out ");"
Finds the smallest key.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_last(const expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t *" key_out ","
.BI "                      uint64_t *" value_out ");"
Finds the largest key.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_next_after(const expanse_map_t *" "map" ", uint64_t "
.BI "key" ","
.BI "                            uint64_t *" "key_out" ", uint64_t *"
.BI "value_out" ");"
Finds the smallest key strictly greater than \fIkey\fR (> key).
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_next_at_or_after(const expanse_map_t *" map ","
.BI "                                  uint64_t " key ", uint64_t *" key_out ","
.BI "                                  uint64_t *" value_out ");"
Finds the smallest key greater than or equal to \fIkey\fR (>= key).
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_prev_before(const expanse_map_t *" "map" ", uint64_t "
.BI "key" ","
.BI "                            uint64_t *" "key_out" ", uint64_t *"
.BI "value_out" ");"
Finds the largest key strictly less than \fIkey\fR (< key).
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_prev_at_or_before(const expanse_map_t *" map ","
.BI "                                  uint64_t " key ", uint64_t *" key_out ","
.BI "                                  uint64_t *" value_out ");"
Finds the largest key less than or equal to \fIkey\fR (<= key).
.SS Rank & Select
.TP
.BI "uint64_t expanse_map_count_below(const expanse_map_t *" map ","
.BI "                                 uint64_t " key ");"
Returns the count of keys strictly less than \fIkey\fR.
.TP
.BI "uint64_t expanse_map_count_range(const expanse_map_t *" map ","
.BI "                                 uint64_t " lo ", uint64_t " hi ");"
Returns the count of keys in the inclusive interval [\fIlo\fR, \fIhi\fR].
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_map_by_count(const expanse_map_t *" map ", uint64_t " n ","
.BI "                          uint64_t *" key_out ", uint64_t *" value_out ");"
Selects the \fIn\fR-th smallest key (1-indexed).
.SS Batched Queries
.TP
.BI "size_t expanse_map_get_batch(const expanse_map_t *" map ","
.BI "                             const uint64_t *" keys ","
.BI "                             uint64_t *" out_values ","
.BI "                             bool *" out_found ", size_t " count ");"
Performs parallel MLP pipelined lookups for \fIcount\fR keys.
